# Line-ending policy
# =================
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites line endings on checkout. That is harmless for source, but it makes
# a byte-for-byte hash of a text file irreproducible: the bytes on disk depend
# on the checkout, not on what was committed.
#
# Two file classes here are hashed or fed to E3D verbatim, so their bytes must
# survive a round trip unchanged.

# Verbatim user evidence. These files record what the user observed in a real
# E3D session and are the basis of every VERIFIED claim in skill/knowledge/.
# tests/test_extrusion_study.py asserts their SHA-256. Never normalised, never
# translated, never reformatted -- see SKILL.md, "Writing language".
Projects/**/results/evidence/** -text

# Verbatim evidence also lives beside archived revisions, not only under
# results/. Any directory named `evidence/` anywhere under Projects/ holds the
# same class of file and gets the same byte-for-byte protection. Added
# 2026-08-18 after Projects/JK-Tank_Build/archive/2026-08-10_top_handrails/
# evidence/ was found uncovered by the results/-only pattern above.
Projects/**/evidence/** -text

# Generated macros and native E3D exports. E3D's macro reader is sensitive to
# stray CR characters, and wsb/pml_compare.py diffs exports line by line.
*.pml -text
*.mac -text

# Syntax-study sources. A study pins its source listing by SHA-256 (see
# tests/test_handra_study.py) exactly as the evidence directories do, but the
# listings are .txt and live under experiments/<STUDY>/source/, which none of
# the patterns above reach. PML-STUDY-HANDRA-001 was committed on 2026-09-09
# with its source unprotected and its hash test passed only in the working tree
# that produced the file -- it failed on the very next checkout, which is the
# failure mode this whole section exists to prevent.
Projects/**/experiments/**/source/** -text

# Native E3D listings supplied by the client. These are verbatim records in the
# same sense as evidence/ -- a study or a reconciliation hashes them to prove it
# read what the client actually sent -- and they are usually .txt, so *.pml does
# not reach them. tests/test_handra_study.py pins the same listing in both its
# imports/ and experiments/ copies.
Projects/**/imports/** -text

# Binary project data, listed explicitly so Git never attempts a text merge.
*.xlsx binary
*.dwg  binary
*.png  binary
